WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.386
This was a town.

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:14.973
Some kind of a
whaling station.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:18.143
Totally abandoned now.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.314
Look at this.

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:25.483
This is what I've been
looking for right here.

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.652
An iron bollard in the shore,

00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:31.406
where Franklin tied
up their ships.

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:35.243
And this was the last anchorage
for the Franklin expedition

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:38.997
before they set off into
the Northwest Passage.

00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:44.002
At that time, sailing over the
top of the world wouldn't have

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:47.922
been too different from the
idea of going to the moon.

00:00:49.674 --> 00:00:53.219
You know, in terms of the
history of exploration,

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:55.346
there's nothing more epic.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.182
You know, almost like a
Knights of the Round table

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:00.518
kind of thing to try to
make it through there.

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:05.315
It's wild to realize that
Franklin and his men were

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:09.194
walking all around here and
preparing for their voyage

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.572
into the Northwest Passage.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.954
From here, the
ice gauntlet begins.

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:32.383
We just sailed
into a fog bank.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.553
This is really really thick.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.681
So I can see about a boat
length and the water is

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:41.434
filled with chunks of ice.

00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:45.105
The radar shows the big stuff,
it shows the bergs,

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:47.941
but it doesn't show
the small stuff.

00:01:47.982 --> 00:01:49.692
It doesn't show the growlers,

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:53.363
and the growlers could
tear the boat in half.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:58.952
Crossing the maze of ice bergs
in Baffin Bay was the first

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:02.580
real test Franklin and his
men faced on their voyage

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.583
into the unknown.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.461
This is part of the reason
why I wanted to sail to

00:02:08.503 --> 00:02:11.965
King William Island, to be
faced with some of the same

00:02:12.006 --> 00:02:17.929
decision points that
Franklin was 175 years ago.

00:02:20.014 --> 00:02:24.477
It was the most modern, the
most well-equipped expedition

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:27.063
in the history of the
world at that point.

00:02:27.105 --> 00:02:30.650
And they
disappeared without a trace.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:36.656
The best way to describe kind
of what it's like out there is

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:39.576
I would call it a
savage wilderness.

00:02:40.618 --> 00:02:41.828
Oh!

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.079
BEN: There it goes!

00:02:43.121 --> 00:02:46.875
Oh man, look at it bouncing!

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:58.511
♪ 

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:02.432
MARK: We can see land!
Woo hoo!

00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:04.184
I have to say, I really
like the place where

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:06.644
the land and sea meet.

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.980
Especially when there's
mountains involved.

